 is really where  you're walking into the park and where  you're seeing everything so I want to  set the best impression over here and  obviously no I didn't really talk about  this yet but um I'm a very firm believer  that courses are built to be looked at  as well which is why I have like the  entire first drop and the looping pretty  much on the full view from the path you  can't really get any closer to it and I  really wanted to make the most use out  of that source of put an extra spotlight  only and now I actually went into the  Christmas strips which should definitely  add a much more Christmassy feel to the  entire build and the there's no real  strategy to this at all I suppose there  was a little bit of research I always do  research - like many of the things I do  or at least I generally know stuff about  them but this was completely new  territory for me actually which sounds  weird and stupid but I've never actually  done like traditional Christmas lights  as you would see that very often I think  American homes do them I'm actually  seeing you know some of these shows on  YouTube which are so amazing where they  actually time the lights and somebody  did this in planet coaster as well I  forgot the name but I'll link it down in  the description there was this awesome  video of somebody doing a a timed  lighting like show on a house in  Christmas style using triggers and it  had over 9,000 triggers I've always been  trying to make a joke here it actually  did and it's absolutely amazing  I'm not doing that kind of thing here  but I wanted to light up the building so  that we actually have a bit of a  Christmas feel to it so that's what I'm  doing here and also some of those  spotlights are kind of slightly  strategically placed because these  lights these light strips don't actually  have like any ambient lights to them but  just a strip of lights but they don't  actually light up their surrounding  areas so I wanted to also focus some  spotlights in the area around those  pieces and actually kind of make it look  as if they are glowing and as if they  are sort of glowing around the area of  the roof which they're placed on and in  some places I just had to play  spotlights on the roof itself just to  light up certain areas of the building  and not leave them in the dark so that  was a bit of interesting work but  generally I'm very happy with how these  lights turn out I think they turn out  fine atmospheric add a lot to the  building especially of night and you  know this is probably the first case  where I think recording at nights for  the final video is gonna be an absolute  focus for me as well like the night time  is something that I haven't gone into as  much so far I've definitely worked with  the lighting before I love the lighting  in the game I think it's one of the  strongest points actually and I've  definitely played around with it in the  past but I just haven't done anything  that's very focused on the the way that  it looks at nights and that is  definitely the case with this coaster so  that's that's a change which is quite  interesting so here still just kind of  like doing all of the different  decorations  they are pretty much all over the place  it's just going to you know any part of  the station just look at it and just  kind of feel you know what could I add  over here is that maybe you'll enter  missing could I add some planters over  here it's just looking around adding  stuff here and there which is very much  just it's just a very primal and error  kind of process with no real thoughts  behind it otherwise and the very final  thing that I wanted to get into before I  get into the next video and I try to do  this as quickly as possible which is why  it might seem like a bit of a cheap  building at this point but finally I  wanted to get into the transfer track  filling or well not really transfer  track building those  which building next to the transfer  track I have a lot of questions about  these things and well I don't want to go  into detail with this the reason that I  am making these is really because it's a  realism issue coaches like these most  coasters in any case usually have a  transfer track and an area like this  where they can store their second train  so in any case usually whenever there is  a coaster with two trains you're going  to want to be able to get one of these  trains off the track and that's why I  have these transfer tracks where you can  drag it onto a separate piece of track  which usually goes into a storage or  maintenance or just a piece of track  where it can be stationed in that and  these are just for you know various  purposes if you don't want to run with  two trains for a time of day or for an  entire day you can store the other train  in there if it needs to be maintained or  taken off that's a way to do it and  that's just I I personally want to add  these things because it's it sort of  gets rid of any necessary potential  suspense of disbelief that you would  need so basically if you're riding this  coaster in planet coaster it could feel  like it's an actual real coaster because  the track looks like a BM the bolts are  there the speed is good the layout is  good you know I don't know exactly say  that but you know what I mean like all  the realistic components are there and  for me having that transfer track at the  end of the track but also seeing it  around the station just adds to the  realism of it and you know kind of makes  it seem like a dream that's closer to  reality than actually being a dream in  the end it's still a game of course it's  not real but it just makes it a bit more  interesting for me and I I feel like  there are quite a few people who agree  with that because I actually remember in  the roller coaster in three days  creating transfer tracks was an art of  its own and something that still right  now even in planning a coaster a lot of  people are very invested in  and it's definitely one of the very  interesting technical components of a  rollercoaster so that's pretty much this  in terms of building though it's very  simple so I wanted to just create a  simple check where the Train could be  and there is pretty much it's and that's  also it for this episode so thank you  guys so much for watching and I hope to  see you guys in the next episode in  which I'll be working on my small huts  and some general surrounding scenery see  you later guys
 

